#: ../eduwifi-watchdog.sh:62
msgid ""
"Usage: %s [command] [options]\n"
"\n"
"Commands:\n"
"  check        Check the Wi-Fi and recover it if needed (default; used by "
"the timer)\n"
"  status       Show Wi-Fi and watchdog status plus the latest events\n"
"  disconnect   Disconnect the Wi-Fi manually; the watchdog will not "
"reconnect until \"on\"\n"
"  off          Turn the Wi-Fi radio off; stays off (even after reboot) until "
"\"on\"\n"
"  on           Turn the Wi-Fi on, re-enable autoconnect and connect to the "
"networks\n"
"  test         Simulate a driver hang and verify the watchdog recovers it "
"(root)\n"
"  gui [ACTION] Desktop dialog used by the menu entry; ACTION is status, off, "
"on or recover\n"
"\n"
"Options for \"check\":\n"
"  --dry-run    Only report what would be done, change nothing\n"
"  --force      Skip straight to reloading the kernel module\n"
"\n"
"Configuration: %s"
msgstr ""
"Uso: %s [orden] [opciones]\n"
"\n"
"Órdenes:\n"
"  check        Comprueba la Wi-Fi y la recupera si hace falta (por defecto; "
"lo usa el temporizador)\n"
"  status       Muestra el estado de la Wi-Fi y del vigilante, y los últimos "
"eventos\n"
"  disconnect   Desconecta la Wi-Fi a mano; el vigilante no la reconectará "
"hasta \"on\"\n"
"  off          Apaga la radio Wi-Fi; sigue apagada (incluso tras reiniciar) "
"hasta \"on\"\n"
"  on           Enciende la Wi-Fi, reactiva la conexión automática y conecta "
"a las redes\n"
"  test         Simula un cuelgue del controlador y comprueba que el "
"vigilante lo recupera (root)\n"
"  gui [ACCIÓN] Diálogo de escritorio que usa la entrada del menú; ACCIÓN es "
"status, off, on o recover\n"
"\n"
"Opciones de \"check\":\n"
"  --dry-run    Solo informa de lo que haría, sin cambiar nada\n"
"  --force      Pasa directamente a recargar el módulo del kernel\n"
"\n"
"Configuración: %s"

